{"name":"Elf Shoe","hex":"#68b082","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being or spirit associated with illness, mischief, and harmful or dangerous magical influence; in later Norse sources, sometimes divided into benevolent light elves (inhabiting  Álfheimr) and malevolent dark elves.","A small, magical creature similar to a fairy, often mischievous, playful, or occasionally helpful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist into elflocks (of hair); to mat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elf"},{"term":"shoe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A protective covering for the foot, with a bottom part composed of thick leather or plastic sole and often a thicker heel, and a softer upper part made of leather or synthetic material. Shoes generally do not extend above the ankle, as opposed to boots, which do.","A piece of metal designed to be attached to a horse's foot as a means of protection; a horseshoe."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put shoes on one's own feet.","To put shoes on someone or something else's feet, especially to put horseshoes on a horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elf","blocks":[{"text":"An elf is a type of humanoid supernatural being in Germanic folklore. Elves appear especially in North Germanic mythology, being mentioned in the Icelandic Poetic Edda and the Prose Edda."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg/330px-%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elf","wikidata":"Q174396"},{"title":"Shoe","blocks":[{"text":"A shoe is an item of footwear normally found in pairs intended to protect and comfort the human foot, usually made in such a way that one is designed to fit the left foot and the other the right foot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg/330px-Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoe","wikidata":"Q22676"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png/500px-Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png/1280px-Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png/500px-Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chart showing how the sound of the word elf has changed in the history of English[2][3]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Alden_Valley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_417197.jpg/500px-Alden_Valley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_417197.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Alden_Valley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_417197.jpg/500px-Alden_Valley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_417197.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alden Valley, Lancashire, a place possibly once associated with elves[13]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlden_Valley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_417197.jpg"},{"srcset